WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.667
-Greg Kinnear, welcome back to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.667 --> 00:00:05.234
It is great to see you
in person.

00:00:05.234 --> 00:00:06.300
-Good to see you.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:07.801
I have an earworm
in my head right now.

00:00:07.801 --> 00:00:09.901
It goes a little something
like this.

00:00:09.901 --> 00:00:12.968
♪ I still
don't understand NFTs ♪

00:00:12.968 --> 00:00:15.000
-I'm telling you, right?
How talented was she, right?

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.968
-It's never going to
leave my mind.

00:00:16.968 --> 00:00:18.934
No, yeah, it's the new
"We Don't Talk About Bruno."

00:00:18.934 --> 00:00:21.434
Yeah, it's giant.
-Yeah.

00:00:21.434 --> 00:00:23.133
-Thanks for being here, bud.
You look great.

00:00:23.133 --> 00:00:25.267
How's the fam?
-Everybody's good.

00:00:25.267 --> 00:00:26.501
Everybody's good.

00:00:26.501 --> 00:00:28.100
We've -- You know,
I haven't seen you

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:30.367
since this whole crazy lockdown

00:00:30.367 --> 00:00:31.801
and everything
we've been through.

00:00:31.801 --> 00:00:34.634
-I'm so happy that you're well.
-Yeah, everybody's good.

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:41.200
I have -- Lockdown
with six daughters is tricky.

00:00:42.601 --> 00:00:43.801
Three daughters, sorry.
-Okay, thank you.

00:00:43.801 --> 00:00:44.801
-Three daughters.

00:00:44.801 --> 00:00:46.567
Felt like six daughters.
-Wow.

00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:49.400
-But, yeah,
we managed to get through it.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:50.634
You have daughters.
-How old are you daughters?

00:00:50.634 --> 00:00:52.067
-They're all teenagers.
[ Audience murmuring ]

00:00:52.067 --> 00:00:54.267
-Wow.

00:00:54.267 --> 00:00:56.534
Yeah, everyone's feeling it.
-That's an appropriate reaction.

00:00:56.534 --> 00:00:57.868
-Everybody -- Wow.

00:00:57.868 --> 00:01:00.100
So three teenage daughters
you were in lockdown with.

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:01.467
-Yes, exactly.

00:01:01.467 --> 00:01:04.934
So we did everything --
My wife and I, we tried to --

00:01:04.934 --> 00:01:08.234
you know, especially in the
early days, we did the dress-up,

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:11.300
we did little bake-offs
before dinner,

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:13.567
and we did culture night.

00:01:13.567 --> 00:01:17.000
And, you know,
it devolved into, you know,

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.734
"Honey, tell the table your

00:01:18.734 --> 00:01:21.868
thorn and rose for the day."

00:01:21.868 --> 00:01:24.267
That's, like, your -- That's
the good thing and bad thing

00:01:24.267 --> 00:01:25.534
that happened to you in the day.

00:01:25.534 --> 00:01:26.834
And they're teenagers.

00:01:26.834 --> 00:01:27.834
They don't want to be asked
that question, Jimmy.

00:01:27.834 --> 00:01:29.133
-No.

00:01:29.133 --> 00:01:31.200
-And I don't know what
a serial killer looks like,

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:34.734
but the looks
that I was getting back.

00:01:34.734 --> 00:01:36.234
-From your own daughters.

00:01:36.234 --> 00:01:38.334
-I mean,
it was -- I had to get out.

00:01:38.334 --> 00:01:40.167
I had to abandon ship

00:01:40.167 --> 00:01:42.200
and find a way out of
the house wherever I could.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:45.801
-Yeah. When they finally
eased up on the lockdown,

00:01:45.801 --> 00:01:49.868
you did something that
I probably would never do.

00:01:49.868 --> 00:01:51.167
-Yeah, I had a friend --

00:01:51.167 --> 00:01:53.033
Well, you would if you were
in my situation.

00:01:53.033 --> 00:01:55.334
I had a friend call me,
and he said,

00:01:55.334 --> 00:02:00.067
"Look, we've got six guys going
about 40 miles off the coast

00:02:00.067 --> 00:02:02.901
of Cuba to go free diving.

00:02:02.901 --> 00:02:05.567
That's diving
without scuba equipment,

00:02:05.567 --> 00:02:06.701
without any apparatus.

00:02:06.701 --> 00:02:09.100
It's open water. It's dangerous.

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:10.567
You're gonna have to sign
a life waiver.

00:02:10.567 --> 00:02:11.601
You could die."

00:02:11.601 --> 00:02:14.234
I was like, "I'm in."

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:15.267
"Get me out of this house."

00:02:15.267 --> 00:02:16.767
-That fast. That fast.

00:02:16.767 --> 00:02:19.434
-Yeah, no, it was really --
But it was crazy.

00:02:19.434 --> 00:02:21.834
At some point --
Because I couldn't get

00:02:21.834 --> 00:02:23.367
as far down as these guys could.

00:02:23.367 --> 00:02:26.434
So I'm in the mid-water.
They're in the deep water.

00:02:26.434 --> 00:02:27.834
Here's the top.
-Yeah.

00:02:27.834 --> 00:02:31.467
-And I'm starting
to see shadows.

00:02:31.467 --> 00:02:34.701
And these are --
these are sharks.

00:02:34.701 --> 00:02:36.968
And they're not -- It's not
just, like, a few sharks.

00:02:36.968 --> 00:02:39.067
It's not like,
"Oh, my God, a shark!"

00:02:39.067 --> 00:02:41.667
There are a plethora of sharks.

00:02:41.667 --> 00:02:43.167
And I wasn't told about it.

00:02:43.167 --> 00:02:45.367
I didn't know about it.
I had no idea about it.

00:02:45.367 --> 00:02:46.434
-What are you talking about?

00:02:46.434 --> 00:02:47.667
-Yeah, there's sharks
in the water.

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:49.801
-I understand,
but that's frightening. What --

00:02:49.801 --> 00:02:51.634
-I don't know how to explain
it any better, Jimmy.

00:02:51.634 --> 00:02:52.968
There's sharks.
-I know, I know. There's sharks.

00:02:52.968 --> 00:02:54.901
But then how do you
get out of there?

00:02:54.901 --> 00:02:58.067
-Well, you have to -- You --
Well, first of all,

00:02:58.067 --> 00:03:02.467
you know, when you do plunge up
and you're struggling for air,

00:03:02.467 --> 00:03:03.534
and the guys come up,
and they're like,

00:03:03.534 --> 00:03:05.000
"Greg, listen, relax.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:07.267
This is their environment.
This is their habitat.

00:03:07.267 --> 00:03:08.901
This is their home."

00:03:08.901 --> 00:03:10.200
And, you know, I'm thinking,

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:11.767
"Well, maybe we
shouldn't be in their home."

00:03:11.767 --> 00:03:13.033
-Yeah.

00:03:13.033 --> 00:03:16.767
-And maybe we should -- But, no,
you have to just realize

00:03:16.767 --> 00:03:19.667
that the fear that you send off

00:03:19.667 --> 00:03:20.834
is the thing that attracts them.

00:03:20.834 --> 00:03:23.300
So you have a, like --
You have an electricity.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:24.801
Jimmy Fallon has electricity.

00:03:24.801 --> 00:03:27.100
-Uh-huh.
-And I think America knows that.

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:29.200
-Thank you.
-But I think --

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:30.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:30.567 --> 00:03:31.767
-I appreciate it.
Thank you very much.

00:03:31.767 --> 00:03:33.534
-I think we've known that.

00:03:33.534 --> 00:03:35.968
So, you can't
turn that electricity off.

00:03:35.968 --> 00:03:39.000
When you're underwater and
you're starting to feel, like,

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:41.367
sharks coming at you, they're --

00:03:41.367 --> 00:03:44.601
You know, that adrenaline
you feel actually sends out

00:03:44.601 --> 00:03:47.634
to these predators a sign
that you're on the menu.

00:03:47.634 --> 00:03:50.100
So it's both good and bad.

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:51.367
-Well, I know you've
won all these awards,

00:03:51.367 --> 00:03:54.634
but, I mean, what --
Can you act not --

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:55.734
You're not fearful at all?

00:03:55.734 --> 00:04:00.100
-I cannot do that.
-You cannot do that.

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:03.467
-I cannot act not fearful.
-Yeah, me neither.

00:04:03.467 --> 00:04:04.868
Yeah, I cannot act not fearful.

00:04:04.868 --> 00:04:08.234
-I not --
I not cannot act fearful.

00:04:08.234 --> 00:04:09.934
-But, so,
you saw these crazy sharks,

00:04:09.934 --> 00:04:11.267
but here's the coolest thing.

00:04:11.267 --> 00:04:13.133
You brought us a video.
-Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:13.133 --> 00:04:15.467
This is --
So, the guy hands me the camera,

00:04:15.467 --> 00:04:17.133
and he says, "I'm gonna go down
with the dudes."

00:04:17.133 --> 00:04:19.300
And he swims down.
I have a camera.

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:22.167
And this is actually --
This is in real time.

00:04:22.167 --> 00:04:23.701
This is a --
-It's a free dive.

00:04:23.701 --> 00:04:25.601
-This is just me
cruising around.

00:04:25.601 --> 00:04:27.167
-No, no, no, no.
-Yeah, so, there --

00:04:27.167 --> 00:04:28.200
-Greg --
-That's --

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:31.100
-Whoa!
Sensed no fear, by the way.

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:33.200
-Yeah, yeah.
-Sensed no fear. Came over.

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:35.901
He's like,
"No, he's cool, he's cool.

00:04:35.901 --> 00:04:38.300
That's frightening.
-Yeah. That's scary stuff.

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:39.834
But that was like --
Honestly, there were --

00:04:39.834 --> 00:04:43.067
It was a lot of sharks.

00:04:43.067 --> 00:04:48.701
So, day four -- They promised
this wouldn't happen.

00:04:48.701 --> 00:04:51.567
I feel a tug
and a sharp thing on my thigh.

00:04:51.567 --> 00:04:54.133
-Stop.
-Bull shark.

00:04:54.133 --> 00:04:57.133
37 stitches on my thigh.

00:04:57.133 --> 00:04:59.334
No, that's bull[bleep]
I just wanted to tell...

00:04:59.334 --> 00:05:01.801
-That's a good actor!

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:03.200
That's a great actor
right there.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:05.501
That's how you do it.
We all fell for it. Oh, my God.

00:05:05.501 --> 00:05:06.634
Bull shark.

00:05:06.634 --> 00:05:07.834
I don't even know
if that's a real shark.

00:05:07.834 --> 00:05:10.133
-I don't think it is.
I don't know.

00:05:10.133 --> 00:05:11.767
As I was down there,
I was like, "You know,

00:05:11.767 --> 00:05:13.868
if there is an upside,
if I were to get bitten,

00:05:13.868 --> 00:05:16.334
it's a great thing
to tell Jimmy."

00:05:17.501 --> 00:05:19.467
-Oh, my gosh. You got me.

00:05:19.467 --> 00:05:22.734
I want to talk about your
new series, "Shining Vale."

00:05:22.734 --> 00:05:23.934
-Yes.
-This is with Courteney Cox.

00:05:23.934 --> 00:05:25.934
-Yes!
-We love Courteney Cox.

00:05:25.934 --> 00:05:27.234
Come on.
-I love Courteney.

00:05:27.234 --> 00:05:30.133
[ Cheers and applause ]
Great.

00:05:30.133 --> 00:05:32.534
-Now, as far as --
There's a part of the show

00:05:32.534 --> 00:05:35.300
where it's horror stuff
in the show.

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:38.367
-Yes. There's horror.
There's comedy.

00:05:38.367 --> 00:05:40.133
There's drama. It's a mystery.

00:05:40.133 --> 00:05:41.501
-Are you easily scared
or just no?

00:05:41.501 --> 00:05:43.200
-You know, I'm not.

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:46.067
Courteney Cox is very --
What a sweetheart.

00:05:46.067 --> 00:05:48.167
I mean, she's so
vulnerable and so easy.

00:05:48.167 --> 00:05:50.133
We're shooting in this,
you know,

00:05:50.133 --> 00:05:53.667
very kind of
scary, gothic house,

00:05:53.667 --> 00:05:56.501
and she genuinely does --
You wouldn't think that,

00:05:56.501 --> 00:05:58.133
'cause she's done,
like, the "Scream" stuff,

00:05:58.133 --> 00:06:01.634
but she's really easy to scare.

00:06:01.634 --> 00:06:04.367
And I got great.
That turned into a sport for me.

00:06:04.367 --> 00:06:06.000
-Oh, yeah.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:08.200
Yeah. You think the
bull-shark story was one thing?

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:09.467
Yeah, wait till you
really get scared by it.

00:06:09.467 --> 00:06:10.634
-Yeah, yeah. It was great.

00:06:10.634 --> 00:06:13.033
-But what can you
tell people about the show?

00:06:13.033 --> 00:06:16.300
-Well, you have to --
I don't actually see the --

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:19.801
It's a family that's in
New York.

00:06:19.801 --> 00:06:23.667
And they --
My wife has had an indiscretion,

00:06:23.667 --> 00:06:26.834
and the family is
trying to rebuild themselves.

00:06:26.834 --> 00:06:27.934
So we move.

00:06:27.934 --> 00:06:29.400
And lot of people
are doing this.

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:31.234
They're moving out of these
big cities into faraway places,

00:06:31.234 --> 00:06:33.634
and what happens is,
your problems follow you.

00:06:33.634 --> 00:06:38.133
So, they move out to
Connecticut, in this house,

00:06:38.133 --> 00:06:39.467
trying to get a new lease.

00:06:39.467 --> 00:06:41.434
And there's a -- She thinks that

00:06:41.434 --> 00:06:43.200
there's something in the house.

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:45.100
I don't believe her.
-Yeah.

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:46.968
-So I don't actually
get to be scared,

00:06:46.968 --> 00:06:49.801
but I'm studying how --
all my scared looks,

00:06:49.801 --> 00:06:52.300
'cause that's
great stuff to do, you know?

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:54.200
-Like, what's a scared --
Like, what?

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:55.834
There's more than
one scared look?

00:06:55.834 --> 00:06:57.534
-Well, there's the standard
horror stuff, like --

00:06:57.534 --> 00:07:00.234
you know, like the quick jump,
and then it's okay,

00:07:00.234 --> 00:07:02.501
where you go --
[ Gasps ]

00:07:02.501 --> 00:07:03.767
You know, that happens
early in the movie.

00:07:03.767 --> 00:07:07.701
And then there's --
[ Laughter ]

00:07:07.701 --> 00:07:10.200
There's the
sound from the other room,

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:11.767
where you're
like -- You have to look --

00:07:11.767 --> 00:07:12.868
It's important
you look this way.

00:07:12.868 --> 00:07:13.901
-Uh-huh.
-And then...

00:07:17.634 --> 00:07:19.801
The eyebrow is key in that.

00:07:19.801 --> 00:07:22.267
You try it.
-Yeah, yeah. Wait. Sorry.

00:07:22.267 --> 00:07:23.667
-You're over here,

00:07:23.667 --> 00:07:25.701
and then you're gonna
hear something over there.

00:07:30.067 --> 00:07:32.801
Okay, that's very good.

00:07:32.801 --> 00:07:34.300
That's very good.

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:37.667
The mother of all, obviously,
is the great horror realization

00:07:37.667 --> 00:07:40.601
that everything you thought
was scary is scary in the house.

00:07:40.601 --> 00:07:43.701
And that requires --
I mean, this is the full Monty.

00:07:43.701 --> 00:07:45.501
So that would
require something like

00:07:45.501 --> 00:07:49.834
you're looking straight ahead,
and then...

00:07:54.968 --> 00:07:56.801
-Oh, my God.

00:07:56.801 --> 00:07:58.567
-You have to --
You have to unhinge.

00:07:58.567 --> 00:07:59.834
-You actually moved your ears.

00:07:59.834 --> 00:08:02.267
-You have to unhinge the jaw.
That's the key.

00:08:02.267 --> 00:08:03.734
-You moved your ears
on that one.

00:08:03.734 --> 00:08:05.100
That was amazing acting
right there.

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:07.634
-If I ever see the ghost in
"Shining Vale," I'm ready.

00:08:07.634 --> 00:08:08.734
I'm ready to go.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:08:08.734 --> 00:08:09.934
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:08:09.934 --> 00:08:12.234
Here is the great
Greg Kinnear and Courteney Cox

00:08:12.234 --> 00:08:13.400
in "Shining Vale."

00:08:13.400 --> 00:08:15.300
Take a look.

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:16.334
-What's up?

00:08:16.334 --> 00:08:17.434
-Nothing, nothing.

00:08:17.434 --> 00:08:18.634
I'm just admiring your

00:08:18.634 --> 00:08:20.801
toddler-trapped-under-a
Toyota-like strength

00:08:20.801 --> 00:08:22.501
and our newly gouged floors.

00:08:22.501 --> 00:08:26.100
-I know you don't want to
hear this, but we have a ghost,

00:08:26.100 --> 00:08:27.501
and I'm pretty sure
she lives in this closet.

00:08:27.501 --> 00:08:28.567
-Oh.

00:08:28.567 --> 00:08:29.567
-Gaynor, I'm sorry to
freak you out.

00:08:29.567 --> 00:08:30.934
-I'm cool.
-Okay, okay.

00:08:30.934 --> 00:08:32.968
Let's -- let's assume
we do have a ghost, Pat.

00:08:32.968 --> 00:08:34.501
And let's say that that ghost
lives right there,

00:08:34.501 --> 00:08:35.767
in this closet.

00:08:35.767 --> 00:08:39.434
Do you really think
that this armoire situation

00:08:39.434 --> 00:08:42.334
is the best way to
keep her from haunting us?

00:08:42.334 --> 00:08:44.400
-Don't condescend.
-Mm-hmm.

00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:46.067
-The armoire's
a stopgap measure.

00:08:46.067 --> 00:08:48.167
-Great. Ghost problem solved.

00:08:48.167 --> 00:08:49.234
Let's have breakfast.

00:08:49.234 --> 00:08:51.200
[ Door creaks ]
-Oh! Aah!

00:08:55.501 --> 00:08:57.501
[ Door creaks ]

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:06.634
-I guess I do get to do it.
I forgot.

00:09:06.634 --> 00:09:09.167
-You Greg Kinnear, everybody!

00:09:09.167 --> 00:09:11.133
"Shining Vale" premieres

00:09:11.133 --> 00:09:14.133
this Sunday at 10:00 p.m.
on Starz.

